WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Settle somewhere safe to pause before you begin.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.750
Let the work wait outside these few minutes.

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.020
You are not falling behind by preparing your attention.

4
00:00:32.005 --> 00:00:33.965
Feel the posture you have brought here.

5
00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:40.015
If it helps, place both feet down and let the spine rise without becoming rigid.

6
00:00:41.715 --> 00:00:44.245
Allow the shoulders to hang from that support.

7
00:01:10.476 --> 00:01:16.826
Notice the residue of what came before: a conversation, a message, another task, or a thought still moving.

8
00:01:18.526 --> 00:01:19.946
You do not need to erase it.

9
00:01:21.646 --> 00:01:23.546
Silently say, that was before.

10
00:01:25.246 --> 00:01:26.516
This is the transition.

11
00:01:57.993 --> 00:02:00.443
Bring attention to the physical sensation of breathing.

12
00:02:02.143 --> 00:02:04.293
Choose one place where the breath is clear enough.

13
00:02:05.993 --> 00:02:09.883
Stay for three cycles, counting each exhale from one to three.

14
00:03:02.344 --> 00:03:06.984
When another concern appears, write it down after the practice if it truly needs remembering.

15
00:03:08.684 --> 00:03:11.164
For now, let it sit at the edge of awareness.

16
00:03:12.864 --> 00:03:14.614
Return to the next exhale.

17
00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.060
Widen attention.

18
00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:57.570
Hear the room.

19
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.980
Feel the whole body sitting here.

20
00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.600
Then narrow attention again to a single point of breath.

21
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:07.840
Wide.

22
00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.860
And narrow.

23
00:04:58.076 --> 00:05:00.966
Focused work does not require shutting out the world by force.

24
00:05:02.666 --> 00:05:07.706
It asks you to recognize what belongs to this period and what can remain outside it.

25
00:05:10.106 --> 00:05:12.186
Name the one piece of work you are about to meet.

26
00:05:13.886 --> 00:05:16.106
Keep it small and concrete.

27
00:05:17.806 --> 00:05:18.876
Not finish everything.

28
00:05:20.576 --> 00:05:27.106
Perhaps read the first page, shape the first paragraph, examine the next result, or make the first decision.

29
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:05.133
Choose a simple way to return when you drift: feel one breath, look again at the question, or place a hand on the desk.

30
00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.453
Drifting will happen.

31
00:06:10.153 --> 00:06:11.923
Returning is the practice.

32
00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.670
Now feel your hands.

33
00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:48.790
Notice the light and the space in front of you.

34
00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.600
Let the eyes focus more clearly.

35
00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Carry one intention into the work: steady, curious, and willing to begin with what is here.
